#EXTINF:472 group-title="T",The Golden Bough Part 2 — James Frazer · VII — OUR DEPT TO THE SAVAGE. General conclusion. Human gods obliged to observe many taboos for their own good and that of their people- These taboos identical with those observed by common people from motives of prudence- A study of these rules afford an insight into the philosophy of the savage- our debt to our savage forefathers. - Read by Leon Harvey - Duration 00:07:52
