#EXTINF:1582 group-title="T",The Golden Bough Part 3 The Dying God — James Frazer · II PART 3. KINGS KILLED AT THE END OF A FIXED TERM. Suicide of the kings of Quilacare at the end of a reign of twelve years- kings of Calicut liable to be attacked and killed by their successors at the end of every period of twelve years- kings of Bengal and Passier and old Slavonic kings liable to be killed by their successors- custom of a five years reign followed by decapitation in Malabar- custom of the Sultans of Java- religious suicides in India- kings killed by proxy- Aun- King of Sweden- and the sacrifice of his nine sons to prolong his life. - Read by Leon Harvey - Duration 00:26:22
